sanctioned: this program uses Db.open + Db.withTransaction + Db.exec (SqlValue params) + Db.findWhere with an Ipe.Db.Unsafe.unsafeFragment-minted WHERE column — the Go reference emits Go+SQLite binaries while Ipê emits Rust+sqlx; the SQLite in-memory behaviour and row-type representation differ enough that a shared Main.ipe cannot run on both backends. Ipê's output is recorded as the correct reference. `unsafeFragment` is an Ipê-only escape hatch (the un-validated anti-Sql.column) with no Go counterpart, so this divergence is structural. The identifier passed here ("qty") is a safe one the caller asserts; the hatch skips valid_sql_ident by design, so the result matches the validated Sql.column path.
